{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Kathryn, for a history project on sports, chronicled the history of college football. When she mentioned that Auburn got cheated out of the NCAA Football championship in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/950877654912421c4311ad620ea305551cdaacfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2004-05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" /> season due to the many flaws in the BCS system, her teacher just couldn’t contain her applause, and awarded an automatic A to her for the rest of the year.\n</p><p>The lecture was so popular, in fact, that many students pressed Kathryn to record the lecture on video and sell DVDs of it.\n</p><p>If the function for Kathryn’s profit for selling DVDs of her college football presentation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9648230a507bec6556cfe59099bb73ed1817d6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -x^2 + 14x + 251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is Kathryn’s profit and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the price per DVD, what price (in dollars) will maximize her profit?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To maximize the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78b9baeda3269077a2ad09186bb8ba6fb0b4182b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^2+14x+251$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, we use the fact that the maximum value of a quadratic occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121cd605cf7dc1e301ccc7c17f9ad3cb39ca2c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the coefficient of the linear term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the leading coefficient. Plugging in the given values, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/1953ac0dc308aa346f7d8e8f45d79ae8a82f4fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{14}{-2}=\\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest\" title=\"2005 iTest\">2005 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 iTest Problems/Prob